# TODO: Translation updated at 2026-09-15 22:29

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:9
translate japanese act2_3615ad1e:

    # nar "You knock once. The door opens before your hand is back at your side."
    nar "一度ノックする。手が体側に戻るより早く、ドアが開く。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:14
translate japanese act2_8e0e450a:

    # m "You came up."
    m "上がってきたのね。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:15
translate japanese act2_909cb681:

    # you "You called the desk."
    you "フロントに電話したのね。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:16
translate japanese act2_6f8ba988:

    # m "People don't always come when you call the desk."
    m "フロントに電話しても、いつも人が来るわけじゃない。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:20
translate japanese act2_e95efd8d:

    # nar "Seven-oh-four is eleven square metres of bed, one chair, and a window that looks straight down onto the street."
    nar "704号室。11平方メートルの空間に、ベッドが一つ、椅子が一つ。窓からは、通りが真下に見える。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:24
translate japanese act2_97067f46:

    # m "He came in, didn't he."
    m "彼、入ってきたんでしょ。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:25
translate japanese act2_1f6605b7:

    # you "Around twenty to four."
    you "三時四十分頃。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:26
translate japanese act2_fdcded8b:

    # m "What did you say?"
    m "何て言った？"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:27
translate japanese act2_7ff2fe80:

    # you "That it had been a quiet night."
    you "静かな夜だったって。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:29
translate japanese act2_471bbdbd:

    # m "You lied to a man you'd never met, for a woman you'd known eight minutes."
    m "会ったこともない男に嘘をついた。たった八分しか知らない女のために。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:30
translate japanese act2_905447cf:

    # you "It wasn't a hard decision."
    you "難しい決断じゃなかった。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:31
translate japanese act2_1d6cf592:

    # m "No. That's the part I'm turning over."
    m "いいえ。そこが、私が考えていることよ。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:34
translate japanese act2_b55cc48e:

    # m "He came in."
    m "彼、入ってきた。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:35
translate japanese act2_465a44fe:

    # you "He did."
    you "ええ。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:36
translate japanese act2_4ff83c39:

    # m "And you showed him the book."
    m "それで、彼に本を見せたのね。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:37
translate japanese act2_e27cd5d9:

    # nar "There is no point in the sentence where you could put a denial."
    nar "その言葉の中に、否定を差し挟む隙はない。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:38
translate japanese act2_13e0b014:

    # you "I did."
    you "そうよ。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:39
translate japanese act2_ed24bcfd:

    # m "Right."
    m "そう。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:41
translate japanese act2_a5242f1c:

    # m "I'm not going to shout at you. You didn't owe me anything. I put money on a counter and asked a stranger to be on my side, and that was optimistic of me."
    m "あなたに怒鳴ったりしないわ。あなたは私に何も借りはない。私はカウンターに金を置いて、見知らぬ人に味方になってくれと頼んだ。それは、私がおめでたかっただけ。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:45
translate japanese act2_5df2544b:

    # m "He came in and you gave him nothing."
    m "彼が入ってくる。あなたは何も与えない。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:46
translate japanese act2_e1e72ab4:

    # you "I gave him the house line."
    you "ハウスラインを出した。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:47
translate japanese act2_dd0c2740:

    # m "The house line is a gift, at four in the morning."
    m "午前四時のハウスラインは、贈り物だ。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:73
translate japanese act2_chair_c08bc8f4:

    # m "Good."
    m "よし。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:74
translate japanese act2_chair_32e33182:

    # you "Good?"
    you "よし、だと？"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:75
translate japanese act2_chair_05ffe937:

    # m "Most men would have sat on the bed."
    m "大抵の男はベッドに座るものだ。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:76
translate japanese act2_chair_aa51e009:

    # nar "You talk. It is four in the morning and neither of you is going to sleep, so you talk."
    nar "言葉を交わす。午前四時。どちらも眠る気配はない。だから、話す。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:80
translate japanese act2_chair_3774e5ee:

    # m "I'm going to ask you something and you can say no and it won't be strange afterwards."
    m "ひとつ、聞きたいことがある。断っても構わない。後腐れはない。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:81
translate japanese act2_chair_acd8b322:

    # m "Stay up here. Not the chair."
    m "ここにいろ。椅子じゃない。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:93
translate japanese act2_bed_b47be58e:

    # nar "You sit on the edge of the bed, close enough that the mattress puts you slightly off balance toward her."
    nar "あなたはベッドの端に座る。マットレスがわずかに傾き、彼女の方へ重心が寄るほど近くに。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:94
translate japanese act2_bed_2aca18d2:

    # m "There we are."
    m "これでよし。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:96
translate japanese act2_bed_2dc1990e:

    # m "Do you want to know the stupid part?"
    m "馬鹿な話、聞きたいか？"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:97
translate japanese act2_bed_ec842a4a:

    # you "Tell me the stupid part."
    you "馬鹿な話を聞かせろ。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:98
translate japanese act2_bed_0e38c0f7:

    # m "I booked a train. It leaves at six-forty. I've had the ticket for nine days and I kept not getting on it."
    m "列車を予約した。六時四十分発だ。九日前から切符を持っていたが、ずっと乗れずにいた。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:99
translate japanese act2_bed_b1381ef4:

    # m "Tonight I got as far as the station and couldn't make myself sit on a bench for four hours where anyone could see me. So I walked, and your doors were the first ones that were open."
    m "今夜も駅までは行った。だが、誰かに見られる場所で四時間もベンチに座っている気にはなれなかった。だから、歩いた。そして、あなたの店が最初に開いていたドアだった。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:100
translate japanese act2_bed_bd70ff42:

    # nar "She turns the bottle in her hands."
    nar "彼女は手の中でボトルを回す。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:101
translate japanese act2_bed_e25eede6:

    # m "So this is the bravest thing I've done in a year. A hotel lobby."
    m "だから、これがこの一年で一番勇敢なことだ。ホテルのロビー。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:102
translate japanese act2_bed_b4c2d737:

    # you "You walked in out of the rain like you owned the place."
    you "雨の中を、まるで自分の場所であるかのように入ってきたな。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:103
translate japanese act2_bed_26c308f1:

    # m "Yes. I'm good at that."
    m "ああ。それは得意だ。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:105
translate japanese act2_bed_bc232ac3:

    # nar "She puts the bottle down on the floor, deliberately, out of the way."
    nar "彼女はボトルを床に置く。わざと、邪魔にならないように。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:106
translate japanese act2_bed_10b72939:

    # m "Ask me to stay awake with you, or tell me to go to sleep. Either one. Just decide, because I've been deciding nothing for eleven months and I'm tired of it."
    m "私に起きていてほしいのか、それとも寝ろと言うのか。どちらでもいい。ただ決めてくれ。この十一ヶ月間、何も決められずにいた。もううんざりだ。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:118
translate japanese act2_window_62f17efe:

    # nar "You stay by the window. The car does not move. Neither does the shape inside it."
    nar "あなたは窓際に立つ。車は動かない。中の影も。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:119
translate japanese act2_window_5aa547ca:

    # m "You can watch him all night. He'll still be there at six."
    m "一晩中、彼を見張っていてもいい。六時にはまだそこにいるだろう。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:120
translate japanese act2_window_08ec6ae1:

    # you "Then at six you'll have a train and he'll have a parking ticket."
    you "そして六時には、あなたは電車に乗り、彼は駐車違反切符を切られる。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:122
translate japanese act2_window_b6192088:

    # m "How do you know about the train?"
    m "どうして電車のことを？"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:123
translate japanese act2_window_b7235d90:

    # you "I don't. It was a guess. Everyone leaving somewhere at this hour has a train."
    you "知らない。勘だ。この時間にどこかへ向かう奴は、みんな電車に乗る。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:124
translate japanese act2_window_4e9213fe:

    # m "Six-forty."
    m "六時四十分。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:127
translate japanese act2_window_8d37aecb:

    # m "Nine days I've had that ticket."
    m "あの切符、九日間持ってた。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:128
translate japanese act2_window_223c2707:

    # nar "Her reflection in the window is looking at yours."
    nar "窓に映る彼女の姿が、あなたの姿を見つめている。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:145
translate japanese act2_decline_51cf8148:

    # m "All right."
    m "わかった。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:159
translate japanese scene_bed_613b1f13:

    # nar "Rain on the window. Neon coming through it in long red bars that move across the sheets when the sign cycles."
    nar "窓に雨。ネオンが長い赤い棒となって差し込み、看板が切り替わるたびにシーツの上を移動する。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:161
translate japanese scene_bed_80f01d26:

    # m "Don't stop."
    m "やめないで。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:177
translate japanese scene_window_99a61c12:

    # m "He can't see up here."
    m "彼はここまでは見えない。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:178
translate japanese scene_window_e5b0b3b1:

    # you "No."
    you "いや。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:179
translate japanese scene_window_c08bc8f4:

    # m "Good."
    m "よし。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:180
translate japanese scene_window_7a085ad0:

    # nar "Four floors down, a man in a car watches a door that nobody comes out of."
    nar "四階下。車中の男は、誰も出てこない扉を見つめている。"

translate japanese strings:

    # game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:56
    old "She has made room on the edge of the bed. The chair is also there."
    new "彼女はベッドの端に場所を空けた。椅子もそこにある。"

    # game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:56
    old "Take the chair."
    new "椅子に座る。"

    # game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:56
    old "Sit next to her."
    new "彼女の隣に座る。"

    # game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:56
    old "Stay standing. Watch the car."
    new "立ったままでいる。車を見張る。"

    # game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:83
    old "She has asked plainly. That deserves a plain answer."
    new "彼女は率直に尋ねた。それには率直な答えが相応しい。"

    # game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:83
    old "Say yes."
    new "「はい」と答える。"

    # game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:83
    old "Say no, and stay in the chair until it's light."
    new "「いいえ」と答え、明るくなるまで椅子に座っている。"

    # game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:108
    old "She has put it in your hands on purpose."
    new "彼女は意図的に、それをあなたに委ねた。"

    # game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:108
    old "\"Stay awake with me.\""
    new "「このまま起きていて」"

    # game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:108
    old "\"Get some sleep. I'll be downstairs.\""
    new "「少し眠るといい。俺は下にいる」"

    # game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:131
    old "She is at the glass beside you. The street is a long way down."
    new "彼女はあなたの隣、窓ガラスの前にいる。通りは遥か下だ。"

    # game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:131
    old "Turn her away from the window."
    new "彼女を窓から遠ざける。"

    # game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:131
    old "Close the curtain and leave her to sleep."
    new "カーテンを閉め、彼女を眠らせておく。"

# TODO: Translation updated at 2026-09-19 01:37

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:8
translate japanese act2_30d12ae8:

    # nar "The fourth-floor corridor smells of old carpet and a cigarette somebody finished three hours ago. The sconce outside 702 has been dying for a year."
    nar "四階の廊下は、古い絨毯と、三時間前に誰かが吸い終えた煙草の匂いがする。702の前の壁灯は、この一年ずっと死にかけている。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:13
translate japanese act2_8adbfac8:

    # nar "The coat is gone. The dress underneath was not chosen for the rain, and it was certainly not chosen for the Marbeck."
    nar "コートはもうない。その下のドレスは、雨のために選ばれたものではなく、ましてマーベックのために選ばれたものでもない。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:21
translate japanese act2_1b5aebf7:

    # nar "The car is still there. From up here you can make out the shape of a man in it, doing nothing, which takes a particular kind of patience."
    nar "車はまだそこにいる。ここからだと、中の男の輪郭が見える。何もしていない。あれには、ある種の忍耐が要る。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:28
translate japanese act2_e539f638:

    # nar "She takes her time with that."
    nar "彼女は、それについて時間をかける。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:40
translate japanese act2_6c6f0ecc:

    # nar "She looks at the window instead of at you."
    nar "彼女はあなたではなく、窓のほうを見る。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:42
translate japanese act2_8cf08b3a:

    # m "But I'll be gone before it's light, and I'd rather not spend my last few hours angry at the only person who's spoken to me today."
    m "「でも明るくなる前には行く。最後の数時間を、今日話した唯一の相手に腹を立てて過ごしたくない」"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:50
translate japanese act2_71cdfbf6:

    # nar "She pours two inches of something into the bathroom tooth glass and hands it to you, then drinks hers from the bottle, which tells you what she thinks of the glass."
    nar "彼女は浴室の歯磨き用コップに二インチほど注いであなたに渡し、自分は瓶から飲む。コップをどう思っているかが分かる。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:52
translate japanese act2_54351b94:

    # m "Sit down. You've been on your feet behind that desk for six hours. I could hear it in how you came up the stairs."
    m "「座って。六時間あのデスクで立ちっぱなしだったでしょう。階段の上がり方で分かった」"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:72
translate japanese act2_chair_5d3ff78e:

    # nar "You take the chair. She watches you do it, and her shoulders come down half an inch."
    nar "あなたは椅子に座る。彼女はそれを見届け、肩が半インチ下がる。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:77
translate japanese act2_chair_ff5b08c3:

    # nar "About the hotel, which has a ghost according to the day porter and a rat problem according to everyone else. About the account with her name on it, and the eleven months it took her to notice she had stopped buying anything she liked."
    nar "ホテルの話。昼番のポーターに言わせれば幽霊がいて、他の全員に言わせればネズミがいる。彼女の名前の口座の話。そして、好きなものを買わなくなっていたと気づくまでにかかった十一か月の話。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:78
translate japanese act2_chair_2b731aba:

    # nar "At some point the bottle is nearly empty and she is on the floor with her back to the bed, near enough that her shoulder rests against your knee."
    nar "いつの間にか瓶はほとんど空で、彼女はベッドに背を預けて床にいる。肩があなたの膝に触れる距離で。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:95
translate japanese act2_bed_6b390c8a:

    # nar "She does not move away. She does not move closer. She lets it sit there being what it is, and drinks, and watches the window."
    nar "彼女は離れない。近づきもしない。その間をそのままにしておいて、飲み、窓を見ている。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:121
translate japanese act2_window_db27c2d7:

    # nar "She laughs. Short, surprised, nothing performed about it — the first one tonight."
    nar "彼女が笑う。短く、不意を突かれた笑い。作ったところがひとつもない——今夜はじめての。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:126
translate japanese act2_window_4d003817:

    # nar "She comes and stands beside you at the glass. Close. The rain has taken the street apart into pieces."
    nar "彼女はガラスの前、あなたの隣に立つ。近い。雨が通りをばらばらに解体している。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:129
translate japanese act2_window_1501b845:

    # m "I don't want to spend the last four hours of it being watched."
    m "「その最後の四時間を、見られて過ごしたくない」"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:144
translate japanese act2_decline_1a0febee:

    # nar "You say the sensible thing. She takes it well, which is worse than if she had not."
    nar "あなたは分別のあることを言う。彼女はそれを感じよく受け取る。怒られるより、そのほうが悪い。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:146
translate japanese act2_decline_be842045:

    # nar "You sit in the chair by the door until the window goes from black to grey. She sleeps eventually, on top of the covers with her shoes on, the way people sleep when they mean to leave."
    nar "あなたは窓が黒から灰色になるまで、ドア脇の椅子に座っている。彼女はやがて眠る。上掛けの上で、靴を履いたまま。出ていくつもりの人間の眠り方で。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:153
translate japanese scene_bed_87a0bb85:

    # nar "The lamp stays on. She reaches past you and turns it to face the wall, so the light climbs the paper instead of crossing the bed — the last ordinary thing either of you does for a long while."
    nar "ランプは点いたままだ。彼女があなたの脇から手を伸ばし、灯りを壁に向ける。光はベッドを横切らず、壁紙を上っていく——それが、しばらくのあいだ二人がする最後の普通のことだ。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:160
translate japanese scene_bed_29fc8317:

    # nar "She is not quiet, and she is not performing not being quiet, and you can hear the difference."
    nar "彼女は静かではない。静かでないことを演じてもいない。その違いは、聞けば分かる。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:162
translate japanese scene_bed_e901750d:

    # nar "Four floors down a car door opens and shuts. Neither of you goes to the window."
    nar "四階下で、車のドアが開いて閉まる。どちらも窓へは行かない。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:170
translate japanese scene_window_a3a086ce:

    # nar "You turn her away from the street, which is what she asked for. She takes two handfuls of your shirt and walks you backwards until the bed stops you, and from there she decides everything, which is also what she asked for."
    nar "あなたは彼女を通りから背けさせる。彼女が求めたとおりに。彼女はあなたのシャツを両手で掴み、ベッドに当たるまで後ろ向きに歩かせる。そこから先は全部彼女が決める。それも、彼女が求めたことだ。"

# game/scripts/02_act2.rpy:176
translate japanese scene_window_9ab74c21:

    # nar "Behind her the window is a sheet of moving water with the city broken up inside it. She does not look at it once."
    nar "彼女の背後で窓は動く水の膜になり、街はその中で砕けている。彼女は一度もそちらを見ない。"

